			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">
<br />

<br />
    Morelen moved quietly through the darkness of the forest.  She disliked this place, found it oddly unbalancing.  Some part of her seemed at home in these woods and that made her angry.  It reminded her of what she was, a half breed, incomplet and half finished.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     She pushed such thoughts to be back of her mind as she focused on her prey.  The young high elven paladin stalked through the woods of Greater Feydark, with the confidence possessd only by one ignorant of the dangers of the world.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     She steped from her hiding place, the crystiline blade glowing darkly in her hand.   
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     &quot;Boy,&quot; She called soflty, &quot;I would have use of you.&quot;  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     Her elvish was accented but good enough to convey her simple needs. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     The young high elf spun, his eyes widdend at the sight of the Tier'Dal standing before him.  His eyes flashed to her black crystal blade and the recognition of what he faced struck him.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
    He brought his blade up as he set his jaw with grim determination. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
    Morelen smiled at him.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
   &quot;I do not seek your life, boy.  Your life would be far to easy for me to take.  I do not butcher children, I measure myself against warriors.&quot;  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     &quot;I simply wish you to carry a message for me.  Within the walls of Felwithe you will find a cadre who call themselves the Concordat Angelis.  Seek the one called Parnhamien and tell him Morelen wishes to speak with him.&quot;   
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
     &quot;And then you, boy should go and test yourself against all these woods have to offer you.  Grow strong, become skilled, learn to wield the power of Tunare and we will finish this dance another day.&quot;  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
       Morelen brings her sword up into a salute even as the shadows seem to flow around her leaveing nothing but darkness in thier wake.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
  /ooc This occurs sometime after Parnhamien's waggon thread at anytime Parnhamien wishes. 
<br />
Morelen Despyte 
<br />

<br />
Shadow Knight of Hate, Lady of Shadows, Bearer of the Book of Dread 
<br />

<br />
House of Dread<i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
