			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Courache runs down the cobblestone streets of Felwithe, apparently being chased by a high elven guard. This alerts the other guards and they join chasing the Teir'Dal as well. Courache yells out behind him as he pants, &quot;I told you already, I just came to visit the Kindred Spirits!&quot; &quot;Bah, probably to slit everyones throat, you Teir'Dal scum!&quot; One of the guards shout back. Courache groans in aggrevasion, and continues running toward the Felwithe gate. The guards pant heavily, and begin to slow down, then come to a stop. He runs past the gate and into the Faydark as the guards yell elvish insults at him. He stops behind a nearby tree, and believes he notices something in the ever looming shadows of the trees. He squints in Parnhamien's direction, but turns and walks away toward Kelethin, relieved the guards ended their pursuit. 
